{"text":"MODEL_FEEDBACK_JSON:
{
  "positive_alignment_reasons": [
    "The microSD cards felt like a natural next choice because I could keep spare Raspberry Pi system images without repurposing my Garmin card.",
    "The portable drive and USB hub support my existing projects: backing up files and connecting my keyboard receiver, card reader, and other laptop accessories."
  ],
  "negative_misalignment_reasons": [
    "The internal SSD, mounting bracket, and SATA dock assume an upgrade or loose drive I do not currently have; working with computers does not mean I need those parts now.",
    "The streaming stick and smart speaker introduce activities I am not pursuing, while the modem assumes a service-equipment replacement that my Ethernet accessories do not establish."
  ],
  "overgeneralized_signals": [
    "My electronics purchases seemed to be treated as interest in almost any connected device, even when it would not help with my current setup.",
    "My use of memory cards seemed to suggest a broader storage upgrade, although spare project cards and an internal 4TB SSD serve very different needs."
  ],
  "missing_or_underweighted_signals": [
    "My recent accessories support connecting, organizing, carrying, and maintaining equipment I already use; practical additions to that setup matter most right now.",
    "An item can fit my setup without being needed: the HDMI cable is relevant, but I already have one, whereas spare project cards would have a distinct use."
  ],
  "summary_diagnosis": "The recommendations recognized my hands-on computer use but stretched it into upgrades and devices without a clear current purpose."
}"}
